Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-ecm: skip the iptables physdev hook on an fw4-only image

The firewall.d hook (qca/feeds/nss/clients/qca-nss-ecm/files/
qca-nss-ecm.firewall) issues two iptables calls before it chooses between
the fw3 and fw4 branches.  This image uses fw4 and ships no iptables
binary, so every firewall (re)start logs three lines:

  procd: /etc/rc.d/S19firewall: sh: /etc/firewall.d/qca-nss-ecm: line 19: iptables: not found
  procd: /etc/rc.d/S19firewall: sh: /etc/firewall.d/qca-nss-ecm: line 20: iptables: not found
  procd: /etc/rc.d/S19firewall: sh: /etc/firewall.d/qca-nss-ecm: line 20: iptables: not found

(line 19 once, line 20 twice because it tests with iptables and then
inserts with it).  The physdev FORWARD rules are iptables-only; fw4
handles bridged traffic in its own table.  Guard the block with
`command -v iptables` so it still runs on an image that has iptables,
and leave the fw3/fw4 branch below untouched -- the nft RATE-LIMIT chain
is what this image actually uses.

---

--- a/qca/feeds/nss/clients/qca-nss-ecm/files/qca-nss-ecm.firewall	2026-11-16 02:22:25.090299197 +0000
+++ b/qca/feeds/nss/clients/qca-nss-ecm/files/qca-nss-ecm.firewall	2026-11-16 02:22:59.103676624 +0000
@@ -16,8 +16,13 @@
 # OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.
 #
 
-iptables -nvL FORWARD | grep -q "physdev" && iptables -Z FORWARD 1
-iptables -nvL FORWARD | grep -q "physdev" || iptables -I FORWARD -m physdev --physdev-is-bridged -j ACCEPT
+# The physdev rules are iptables-only.  An fw4-only image has no iptables
+# binary, and the two unconditional calls above the branch below fail with
+# "iptables: not found" on every firewall (re)start.
+if command -v iptables >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+	iptables -nvL FORWARD | grep -q "physdev" && iptables -Z FORWARD 1
+	iptables -nvL FORWARD | grep -q "physdev" || iptables -I FORWARD -m physdev --physdev-is-bridged -j ACCEPT
+fi
 
 if grep -q "fw3" /etc/init.d/firewall; then
 	iptables -nvL | grep -q "Chain RATE-LIMIT" && iptables -F RATE-LIMIT
